      "title": "Adjunct- Art and Science of Cannabis Extraction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\n\nLocation: Scranton\n\nLACKAWANNA COLLEGE HAS BEEN VOTED ONE OF THE “BEST PLACES TO WORK IN PA” FOR 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2019, 2020, 2023, 2024 and 2025!   Lackawanna College is a private, accredited college serving the people of Northeastern Pennsylvania. Our main campus is located in downtown Scranton, and our footprint includes satellite centers in  Covington Twp. ,  Hawley ,  Hazleton ,  Sunbury ,  Towanda  and  Tunkhannock   Our mission is to provide a quality education to all persons who seek to improve their lives and better the communities in which they live.  We provide our students with a direct path to a bachelor’s degree, associate degree, or one of many different professional certifications. Additionally, our  Continuing Education department  helps put the people of Northeastern Pennsylvania back to work with modern career skills.  Lackawanna is also one of the  most cost-efficient  regional higher education institutions.   If our mission inspires you, and you are willing to go the extra mile to help our students succeed, please feel free to apply for this or future employment opportunities for which you meet the minimum qualifications. Please know that only the candidates who meet the minimum qualifications can be considered, and only those selected for interviews will be contacted by a college representative.  No phone calls, please . _______________________________________________________________________________________ Adjunct Instructor – Art and Science of Cannabis Extraction This course is part of our Online Cannabis Professional Certificate.  ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS, PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES AND OBJECTIVES: Adjunct instructors are part-time faculty hired to teach a specified course/s on a per-semester basis. The opportunity to continue teaching at the college is assessed every semester, and criteria for re-employment include: Attention to administrative deadlines (i.e., setting up course prior to semester start, grading student work, tracking attendance), timely and professional communication with students and colleagues, and students’ course/instructor evaluations. Current openings are for classes running online (virtual) for fall 2026.  ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Prepares lesson plans and instructs students in a classroom and/or virtual (TEAMS) setting. Thoroughly prepares and teaches all course lessons, considering diverse learners and accounting for current trends and industry regulations. Provides support and guidance to students to optimize learning outcomes. Completes and maintains all required documentation and records, meeting established deadlines, including, but not limited to, syllabi, grades, midterm and final grades, attendance, and end-of-semester reflection on Student Learning Objectives (SLOs). Fosters a professional and supportive classroom environment conducive to students learning, asking questions, thinking critically, and growing as individuals. Provides meaningful hands-on application of material to reinforce transfer of learning. All other duties as required by the Dean. KEY COMPETENCIES: Demonstrated sensitivity in working with students of diverse backgrounds. Ability to adapt instructional methodologies for different learning styles. Ability to work independently and conscientiously. Excellent computer skills. Ability to prioritize and multitask responsibilities. Proficient written and verbal communication skills. Effective interpersonal skills, demonstrating empathy and encouragement.  Willingness to work collaboratively with internal and external partners of the business division and the College. Commitment to fulfillment of the College mission.   EDUCATION: Bachelor’s degree required. Coursework in chemistry and Cannabis Extraction preferred. Professional work and field experience preferred. Master’s degree preferred.   EXPERIENCE: Demonstrated prior teaching experience in a corporate or higher education setting preferred. Proficiency using Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas). ______________________________________________________________________________________   In compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and all other applicable non-discrimination laws, Lackawanna College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran’s status, or genetic information in its educational programs and activities, admissions, and with regard to employment. Lackawanna College is an accredited, private, non-profit educational institution providing opportunities for career and personal development within selected associates degree, certificate and continuing education program.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9d114fa5-887f-4687-9b71-ee538589a4bb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9203058799873_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Grad Assistant Graduate Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\n\nLocation: Scranton\n\nJob Title: Graduate Assistant (Grad Focus) Department: Graduate Studies Reports to: Dean of Graduate Studies Position Type: Eighth-Time (5 hours/week)  Duration: 2627 Job Summary: The Graduate Assistant (GA) will assist faculty and staff in Graduate Studies with various tasks related to research, teaching, and administrative support. The position offers graduate students the opportunity to gain professional experience while pursuing advanced studies. The GA will work closely with faculty members and staff to support departmental goals, foster academic engagement, and contribute to the overall success of departmental initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Course Design Support: Assist in maintaining accuracy and consistency across graduate-level courses in Canvas, while aiding implementation of the FALCONS model. Graduate Studies Ambassador:Represent and promote Peirce at Lackawanna’s graduate programs by serving as a liaison between prospective students and the college, sharing their experiences and insights to support recruitment, orientation, and community engagement efforts. Student Support Services & Academic Advising:Communicate with students and collaborate with Graduate Academic Advisors to ensure timely support for continued enrollment and financial aid needs. Assisting in Event Execution: Support the planning and execution of various events such as graduate new student orientation and events (i.e., Elevate Series, CEOSpotlightand Instant Decision Day). This involves coordinating logistics, managing registrations, and ensuring smooth operations during the events. Collaborating with Stakeholders: Work closely with faculty, staff, and the Graduate Student Association to organize events that align with the goals of the graduate studies programs. Qualifications: Enrolled/accepted in a graduate degree program at Lackawanna College Strong academic standing Excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team setting Possessstrong organizational and time-management skills In accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and institutional policies, you are required to: Maintain Confidentiality: Ensure that all student records and related information are kept confidential and are not disclosed to unauthorized individuals. Access on a Need-to-Know Basis: Use student information solely for the purposes of fulfilling your GA responsibilities.  Secure Handling: Store and transmit student data securely, following best practices to prevent unauthorized access or breaches. Report Violations: Immediately report any suspected breaches of confidentiality or privacy to your supervising faculty member or the appropriate institutional office. Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with MS Office, including Teams. Ability to adapt to a fast-paced and dynamic academic environment.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9d114fa5-887f-4687-9b71-ee538589a4bb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202999966188_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Grad Assistant eLearning Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-22\n\nLocation: Scranton\n\nJob Title: Graduate Assistant (GA) - Remote Department: eLearning Reports to: Associate Dean of eLearning Position Type: Eighth Time – 5 hours per week Duration:  Academic Year 2026-2027 Job Summary   The Graduate Assistant (GA) supports faculty and staff in the eLearning Department with a variety of tasks related to research, teaching, and administrative duties. This role provides graduate students with valuable professional experience while they pursue their advanced studies. The GA collaborates closely with faculty and staff to help achieve departmental objectives, encourages academic involvement, and contributes to the success of departmental initiatives.  Key Responsibilities  Instructor Support:Provide support to instructors by triaging questions andassistingwith Canvas course setup and ongoing course management. Responsibilities include organizing course content, uploading materials, creating assignments and discussions, and offering basic troubleshooting to ensure courses are set up effectively. Administrative Tasks: Help organize departmental events, workshops, and conferences. Provide general administrative assistance, including responding to emails, scheduling meetings, maintaining records, and updating databases.  Research/Data Support: Assist with data collection specific to each department  Other Duties:Complete additional tasks asassigned by the department, faculty, or supervisor that support professional development and academic goals.  Peak Times:Works during high impact periods, which include, but are not limited to: annual forum, graduation, orientations, week prior to the start of the semester, first two weeks of the semester, last two weeks of the semester prior to finals, and advising periods.   Qualifications  Enrollment/accepted in a Lackawanna College graduate program in Higher Education, Organizational Leadership & Management, Professional Studies, or MBA   Strong academic standing.  Excellent written and oral communication skills.  Proficiencywith Microsoft Outlook,Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, and Excel, as well as experience with Canva, Canvas LMS, and OneDrive. Ability to work independently and as part of a team.  Strong organizational and time-management skills .",
      "department": ""
    },
